WEBVTT

00:01.060 --> 00:03.030
I'm going to enter the Joust too.

00:03.900 --> 00:05.870
I want to enter.

00:09.100 --> 00:12.730
It will all be mine, the land and the
glory of the championship.

00:17.280 --> 00:19.250
What do you think you're doing?

00:20.420 --> 00:22.210
No, wait!

00:24.790 --> 00:32.530
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

00:32.530 --> 00:39.490
Towards a far, faraway place

00:52.850 --> 00:59.050
Blown by the wind, we walk on

00:59.050 --> 01:06.020
Wanting to know the reason we were born

01:06.230 --> 01:12.530
Even if a time of loss should come

01:12.530 --> 01:19.670
Let's now choose to hold each other tight

01:22.110 --> 01:29.520
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

01:29.520 --> 01:35.490
Towards something we can't lose

01:35.490 --> 01:43.130
Pulling only brilliant dreams closer

01:43.130 --> 01:50.000
Towards a far, faraway place

02:10.230 --> 02:12.350
Is Zed going to be okay?

02:13.230 --> 02:16.030
Well, there's no way he can win
against Master Robès.

02:16.560 --> 02:18.190
Begin!

02:29.580 --> 02:31.550
You're not so tough.

02:39.920 --> 02:44.150
Episode 5
The Nation of Sacred Law

02:52.470 --> 02:54.590
Oh, thank goodness!

02:55.400 --> 02:57.200
How do you feel?

02:58.370 --> 03:02.170
Where am I?

03:06.680 --> 03:08.650
Here, have some.

03:13.320 --> 03:16.450
Eat it all up and get well, okay?

03:17.830 --> 03:20.920
Oh, I'll go get you some fruit.

03:24.000 --> 03:26.700
"Get well"?

03:26.700 --> 03:30.070
I didn't know I was still alive.

04:06.910 --> 04:08.540
Zed!

04:11.280 --> 04:13.650
Zed... I've got to rescue him!

04:49.020 --> 04:51.320
The patient disappeared while in transport!

04:52.520 --> 04:54.090
Yes, we searched for him.

04:54.090 --> 04:56.060
He's not anywhere to be found!

05:03.700 --> 05:05.500
Easy there!

05:07.870 --> 05:10.240
Lady Diana...

05:10.240 --> 05:12.610
Did you succeed in your summoning?

05:12.610 --> 05:14.080
Yes...

05:14.080 --> 05:16.980
But we do not know which area he's arrived in.

05:16.980 --> 05:20.540
But there is no doubt he is within
our own territory, correct?

05:20.920 --> 05:22.880
That much is certain.

05:24.720 --> 05:26.420
Well done.

05:26.420 --> 05:28.650
The rest is my job.

05:36.330 --> 05:38.630
Ah, the land is finally cleared and ready.

05:38.630 --> 05:40.030
Finally!

05:40.030 --> 05:41.500
Honey!

05:41.500 --> 05:42.140
Look...

05:42.140 --> 05:43.600
What's the matter?
Look...

05:44.770 --> 05:46.400
Oh, dear...

05:51.480 --> 05:54.040
What is this light?

05:57.150 --> 05:59.380
You're all right now.

06:14.440 --> 06:17.230
Where am I?

06:20.480 --> 06:24.340
That light... what in the world was it?

06:26.110 --> 06:27.680
How are you feeling?

06:27.680 --> 06:29.250
I've made some soup for you.

06:29.250 --> 06:30.750
Think you'd be able to eat some?

06:30.750 --> 06:32.790
I can do my best to shard-heal you,

06:32.790 --> 06:35.190
but you need to do your part to
keep up your strength.

06:35.760 --> 06:37.380
Shard?

06:38.230 --> 06:39.850
Um...

06:41.560 --> 06:43.360
Uh, nothing.

06:44.730 --> 06:47.940
One who will save this country?

06:47.940 --> 06:50.610
Is he really such an individual?

06:50.610 --> 06:54.100
It seems so to Master Tokiyomi's clairvoyant eye.

06:55.980 --> 06:58.810
I am not yet able to draw my own conclusions.

06:58.810 --> 07:01.440
Do as you will.

07:02.450 --> 07:05.590
As you command, Your Holiness.

07:05.590 --> 07:09.820
In the name of Absolute Justice,
and for the future of Neotopia.

07:18.170 --> 07:20.770
These shards are amazing.

07:20.770 --> 07:22.900
I can't believe how energetic I feel.

07:24.470 --> 07:25.940
I may be able to heal your wounds,

07:25.940 --> 07:29.480
but I'm afraid I can't completely heal your body.

07:29.480 --> 07:30.850
You've done more than enough.

07:30.850 --> 07:33.140
I am truly indebted to you.

07:34.120 --> 07:35.740
Noah...

07:36.150 --> 07:37.850
Do you have anywhere to go?

07:37.850 --> 07:39.480
Um, well, no.

07:39.790 --> 07:43.320
Then, why don't you stay here
with us for a while?

07:43.320 --> 07:47.200
But I can't allow myself to be
any more of a burden...

07:47.200 --> 07:49.160
We don't mind at all!

07:49.660 --> 07:53.600
We actually have a son who's about your age.

07:53.600 --> 07:57.000
He's off at the capital doing
his military service now.

07:57.910 --> 08:01.910
Say, you know it's not as interesting,
just the two of us here alone, is it?

08:01.910 --> 08:03.180
What do you say, Noah?

08:03.180 --> 08:06.710
If it's all the same to you, then by
all means, feel free to stay here

08:06.710 --> 08:10.120
for as long or short a time as you like. Right?

08:10.120 --> 08:13.220
Of course! Even if it's just until you
know where you're going.

08:13.220 --> 08:15.020
How about that?

08:15.690 --> 08:17.660
Thank you very much.

08:21.430 --> 08:26.730
It looks like this is an entirely different
world than where I've come from.

08:27.440 --> 08:29.400
But how...

08:41.520 --> 08:44.040
Thanks for the help, Noah.

08:45.050 --> 08:46.050
No problem.

08:46.050 --> 08:49.550
You know, this sure is nice, building
a park from scratch and all.

08:50.260 --> 08:55.700
I've long dreamed of one day building
a park filled with greenery.

08:55.700 --> 08:57.530
A park, huh?

08:57.530 --> 09:00.640
Ever since I was little, I've always
been weak and frail,

09:00.640 --> 09:03.760
so I never really got to play in the park much.

09:05.640 --> 09:09.800
Then, I guess you ought to be the first to
ride the swings when we're done.

09:11.250 --> 09:12.850
Good call!

09:12.850 --> 09:15.680
I'll push you.

09:16.220 --> 09:17.920
Oh, no, that's okay!

09:17.920 --> 09:19.890
I'm not a kid anymore after all.

09:20.450 --> 09:24.030
Noah's kind of like Gale in a way, isn't he?

09:24.030 --> 09:25.030
Gale?

09:25.030 --> 09:26.430
That's my son.

09:26.430 --> 09:28.400
C'mon, let's bring the logs over.

09:28.400 --> 09:30.020
Sure!

09:40.170 --> 09:43.410
What? You mean your not building
the park as part of your job?

09:44.180 --> 09:45.780
More of a hobby, I'd say.

09:45.780 --> 09:47.820
That's no way to put it!

09:47.820 --> 09:49.380
Oh, dear me.

09:49.380 --> 09:51.920
The name of this village is Ratt.

09:51.920 --> 09:55.420
In the past, we made a large
contribution to the government.

09:55.420 --> 10:00.260
Thanks to that, the government now takes care
of virtually every aspect of our daily lives.

10:00.260 --> 10:02.260
I see...

10:02.260 --> 10:07.800
So, we're free to use our time
to do whatever we like.

10:07.800 --> 10:10.810
And if that time is spent in service
to our village and country,

10:10.810 --> 10:13.370
we simply couldn't be happier.

10:13.370 --> 10:18.350
There's a monument constructed atop the hill,
built in honor of those past achievements.

10:18.350 --> 10:19.880
The view up there is wonderful too.

10:19.880 --> 10:21.450
Why not go have yourself a look?

10:21.450 --> 10:25.220
This land of Neotopia is a truly wonderful country.

10:25.920 --> 10:27.550
Neotopia...

10:32.890 --> 10:34.600
Is this it?

10:34.600 --> 10:36.590
Is this the monument?

10:40.500 --> 10:42.470
What do you want?

10:43.940 --> 10:45.740
What are you doing?!

10:47.270 --> 10:49.380
I saw you in the park yesterday...

10:49.380 --> 10:51.900
What are you trying to find out?
Who sent you?

10:53.410 --> 10:56.180
Who the heck are you?!

10:56.680 --> 10:59.310
I was just here to see the monument!

11:00.020 --> 11:01.990
You're not fooling me!

11:02.490 --> 11:04.530
What is going on here?

11:04.530 --> 11:06.150
My body...

11:06.960 --> 11:08.930
...is moving exactly where I envision it moving.

11:10.360 --> 11:12.160
Stop dodging me!

11:13.130 --> 11:15.430
Who in his right mind would stand
still so you could hit him?!

11:25.010 --> 11:28.000
Guess I'm not cured after all...

11:29.850 --> 11:31.650
Hey, what's with you?

11:32.120 --> 11:33.920
Keith!

11:33.920 --> 11:36.550
Pull it together!
Hey! What's wrong with you?

11:42.630 --> 11:45.300
You'll have to receive healing periodically.

11:45.300 --> 11:46.570
If you don't, then...

11:46.570 --> 11:48.240
I know.

11:48.240 --> 11:50.600
I've been like this since birth.

11:50.600 --> 11:54.580
Sheesh, I figured you were some
military or government dog.

11:54.580 --> 11:55.680
Keith!

11:55.680 --> 11:58.510
No one like that would come to our village!

11:59.250 --> 12:01.950
Sorry about him, he's really not that bad.

12:01.950 --> 12:03.850
Hey, say...

12:03.850 --> 12:06.550
You're not from Neotopia, are ya?

12:06.550 --> 12:08.420
Where'd you come from?

12:08.420 --> 12:10.930
Templar? Zymot?

12:10.930 --> 12:12.530
Um, well...

12:12.530 --> 12:16.860
I think this is probably a completely
different world from my own.

12:20.270 --> 12:23.600
The world I was in is called Calm.

12:29.140 --> 12:31.610
Are you kidding me? That's totally wild!

12:32.580 --> 12:35.310
A completely different world from this one?

12:36.520 --> 12:38.490
I want to go check that out!

12:40.920 --> 12:43.120
Kind of like someone I know...

12:46.990 --> 12:48.130
Zed...

12:48.130 --> 12:49.860
I found him passed out again.

12:49.860 --> 12:51.830
He had me scared.

13:02.410 --> 13:06.710
So, this boy really passed out before the Ark?

13:06.710 --> 13:07.920
That's right.

13:07.920 --> 13:10.440
And boy was he heavy!

13:12.020 --> 13:15.350
The Ark reacted to this young man?

13:23.930 --> 13:25.730
No, it couldn't be.

13:27.230 --> 13:28.240
Noah!

13:28.240 --> 13:29.300
Keith?

13:29.300 --> 13:30.700
Where ya going?

13:30.700 --> 13:33.240
To help work on the park.

13:33.240 --> 13:35.900
You can slack off today. C'mon!

13:39.750 --> 13:41.320
Get back here you!

13:41.320 --> 13:42.650
Whoa!

13:42.650 --> 13:44.280
W..Wait!

13:53.590 --> 13:55.220
C'mon, man!

13:56.400 --> 13:58.020
No, I couldn't...

14:26.430 --> 14:28.630
I haven't had this much fun in a long time.

14:28.630 --> 14:29.630
Same!

14:29.630 --> 14:30.970
How are you feeling?

14:30.970 --> 14:32.500
I'm all right.

14:32.500 --> 14:34.130
That's great!

14:35.640 --> 14:38.240
It kind of seems like the old days.

14:38.240 --> 14:42.080
Yeah, it's like Gale came back.

14:42.080 --> 14:44.980
Gale? You mean Carter's son?

14:44.980 --> 14:48.020
That's right, the three of us are childhood friends.

14:48.020 --> 14:49.950
He's a hell of a guy!

14:49.950 --> 14:54.250
We'd always come stargazing like this
after we'd had our fun.

14:58.090 --> 15:01.600
Noah, what do you think of this country?

15:01.600 --> 15:03.660
I like it quite a lot.

15:03.660 --> 15:06.570
It's calm and quiet, and all the people are so nice.

15:08.740 --> 15:10.470
That right?

15:25.190 --> 15:26.650
Hey, give me that.

15:26.650 --> 15:29.250
I'm amazed how delighted they are.

15:34.460 --> 15:37.830
It looks like you've been getting
to know Keith, huh?

15:37.830 --> 15:40.070
Huh? Yes...

15:40.070 --> 15:42.400
Better to steer clear of him.

15:42.400 --> 15:44.240
He refuses to do his military service.

15:44.240 --> 15:46.260
Truly hopeless, that one.

15:47.440 --> 15:52.170
I simply can't comprehend the way he thinks.

15:59.520 --> 16:01.150
Hey, guys.

16:02.290 --> 16:05.460
Well? You decided?

16:05.460 --> 16:07.630
Nah, sorry, man.

16:07.630 --> 16:09.030
No problem.

16:09.030 --> 16:14.770
For better or worse, the spirit of this country
has been fully pounded into us.

16:14.770 --> 16:15.900
Right...

16:15.900 --> 16:17.530
This way.

16:39.230 --> 16:40.850
That guy...

16:53.440 --> 16:55.410
Aren't you going back?

16:56.040 --> 16:58.200
Now's not the best time...

16:59.810 --> 17:01.440
Oh?

17:03.180 --> 17:04.220
You don't say!

17:04.220 --> 17:05.850
I see!

17:09.290 --> 17:10.920
Gale!

17:11.260 --> 17:13.030
Long time no see!

17:13.030 --> 17:15.060
Keith! And Aisha!

17:15.060 --> 17:17.330
Welcome home, Gale!

17:17.330 --> 17:18.730
Thanks for coming by.

17:18.730 --> 17:21.370
Thanks for never even writing, jerk!

17:21.370 --> 17:23.170
Sorry, sorry.

17:30.440 --> 17:31.810
You look well.

17:31.810 --> 17:33.750
Are you home on leave?

17:33.750 --> 17:34.950
Yeah...

17:34.950 --> 17:37.580
So, what's the capital like, Gale?

17:37.580 --> 17:40.150
I find enrichment in my daily
service to the country.

17:40.150 --> 17:41.160
Oh yeah?

17:41.160 --> 17:43.860
What have you been up to, Keith?

17:43.860 --> 17:46.720
Huh? Me? Nothing much.

17:47.530 --> 17:51.800
You indulge in the benefits this country
provides, but refuse military service.

17:51.800 --> 17:55.440
As a citizen of Neotopia,
don't you feel any shame at all?

17:55.440 --> 17:56.970
Gale!

17:56.970 --> 17:58.770
Let's not talk about that.

17:58.770 --> 18:01.240
So, what are you doing now?

18:02.610 --> 18:04.810
Aren't you doing anything?

18:04.810 --> 18:08.180
Are you just idling the days away?

18:08.180 --> 18:10.810
Wouldn't that make you human debris?

18:11.390 --> 18:13.010
Keith!

18:17.360 --> 18:20.330
Gale, you've changed.

18:20.330 --> 18:23.320
What is it? What happened?

18:25.630 --> 18:27.170
Nothing at all.

18:27.170 --> 18:29.330
I'm just disappointed in you.

18:30.970 --> 18:33.210
Keith! Are you okay?

18:33.210 --> 18:34.940
Keith...

18:34.940 --> 18:36.570
Gale!

18:42.020 --> 18:43.640
Gale...

18:54.730 --> 18:56.360
Wow!

18:59.630 --> 19:01.600
It's amazing!

19:01.600 --> 19:03.400
They're moonbeam flowers.

19:03.400 --> 19:09.380
When the air is just right and the
moonlight strikes just so, they glow.

19:09.380 --> 19:14.140
When we were young, we'd often come here
and wait for the flowers to open.

19:29.500 --> 19:32.900
We did everything together, the three of us.

19:32.900 --> 19:37.240
Keith and Gale were especially close,
like brothers almost.

19:37.240 --> 19:42.110
I really loved being in the middle
of that relationship.

19:47.510 --> 19:52.580
Can't things ever go back to how they were then?

19:55.320 --> 19:56.720
Where's Noah?

19:56.720 --> 19:59.780
He hasn't come back from Keith's.

20:01.460 --> 20:02.660
I see...

20:02.660 --> 20:03.660
Noah?

20:03.660 --> 20:06.260
Oh, he's a very nice boy who's a lot like you.

20:07.070 --> 20:09.400
He's living with us now.

20:17.110 --> 20:18.210
Well, all right then.

20:18.210 --> 20:20.180
You're the one called Noah, right?

20:21.450 --> 20:23.510
We are taking you into custody.

20:25.290 --> 20:26.020
Where are you taking me?

20:26.020 --> 20:27.120
Just come along quietly.
Where are you taking me?

20:27.120 --> 20:28.750
Just come along quietly.
What have I done?

20:29.760 --> 20:32.360
Rescuing and providing shelter to a man
who had collapsed in the street

20:32.360 --> 20:34.760
is a praiseworthy deed.

20:36.700 --> 20:37.730
Gale?

20:37.730 --> 20:42.830
But do praiseworthy deeds entitle us
to neglect the law of the land?

20:43.800 --> 20:44.970
Nay!

20:44.970 --> 20:50.470
Holding the law in contempt for any reason
whatsoever is an act of depravity!

20:51.110 --> 20:55.420
When you come across an individual of
unknown origin, you report this to the capital.

20:55.420 --> 20:58.050
This is a fundamental law.

20:58.050 --> 21:00.780
This man disregarded that law!

21:03.920 --> 21:05.550
Carter!

21:06.160 --> 21:09.260
Keith! Something awful has happened!

21:09.260 --> 21:11.800
It's Noah... Noah's in trouble!

21:11.800 --> 21:13.430
What?!

21:13.430 --> 21:18.740
Neotopia's ideal is the greatest
happiness for all citizens.

21:18.740 --> 21:23.570
Observance of strict laws is precisely what
will enable us to achieve this ideal.

21:26.080 --> 21:28.450
No, you're not going to...

21:28.450 --> 21:30.420
There's no way, right?

21:32.390 --> 21:35.860
You're telling me he didn't submit a report?!

21:35.860 --> 21:37.660
What a frightful thing he's done!

21:37.660 --> 21:40.290
How could he break the law?

21:42.900 --> 21:44.520
Gale!

21:47.270 --> 21:48.890
Carter!

21:52.440 --> 21:55.240
Please let go! This is insane!

21:55.240 --> 21:56.110
I've got to stop him!

21:56.110 --> 21:58.010
Stop struggling!
I've got to stop him!

21:58.010 --> 22:01.210
Let go! We've got to help Carter!

22:08.890 --> 22:10.690
Why?

22:10.690 --> 22:13.290
How can you be smiling?!

22:23.000 --> 22:26.100
In the name of Absolute Justice,
I now punish you.

22:28.310 --> 22:32.510
Stop it!

22:50.500 --> 22:54.370
I want to peak inside your heart, and find
out your feelings and expressions

22:54.370 --> 22:58.270
I see you bearing your burden alone, and don't
ask the reason for your twinkling tears

22:58.270 --> 23:01.840
I give you a shout of support without mentioning
them, between the answers I'm looking for

23:01.840 --> 23:05.970
Without obsessing or over thinking,
I feel sunbeams in the future you

23:07.680 --> 23:09.520
It feels nice, very, very much

23:09.520 --> 23:11.320
You and me, we're very, very good

23:11.320 --> 23:15.190
I'd like to be there for you any time

23:15.190 --> 23:17.020
Very, very much, whenever

23:17.020 --> 23:18.860
Very, very good, not changing

23:18.860 --> 23:24.820
We're always blooming full of hope,
with all our might (Oh)

23:30.340 --> 23:32.810
I feel this kindness amidst my doubt

23:34.110 --> 23:36.580
I will always have faith in you at all times

23:37.840 --> 23:41.750
Here in this vast landscape
under the sunny blue sky

23:41.750 --> 23:45.880
We got good feelings, good social standing,
we're good; I want to always be here

23:47.350 --> 23:49.160
It feels nice, very, very much

23:49.160 --> 23:50.990
You and me, we're very, very good

23:50.990 --> 23:54.800
I'd like to be there for you any time

23:54.800 --> 23:56.660
Very, very much, whenever

23:56.660 --> 23:58.530
Very, very good, not changing

23:58.530 --> 24:04.490
We're always blooming full of hope,
with all our might (Oh)

24:16.020 --> 24:19.950
Next Time
A Rushed Concluion

24:16.980 --> 24:19.950


Next time, "A Rushed Conclusion"
